 },
 "method": {
  "led_check": "led_check.py, run from RAM with `mpremote connect id:e6647c15673a2438 run led_check.py` (interrupts main.py). Sensor() built as main.py builds it: 128x (code 8), ATIME 100, ASTEP 999. LED via lib/as7341.py set_led_current(mA), which allows 4-20 mA. Each block repeated at 32x (code 6) when saturated. LED off in a finally block.",
  "led_hold": "led_hold.py: LED on at 4 mA for 20 s while the robot camera took a photo, then off",
  "restore": "`mpremote ... reset` (hard reset; main.py runs from flash and its Sensor() re-init also clears CONFIG), then plain 128x reads over MQTT",
  "registers": "CONFIG 0x70 bit 3 = LED_SEL, LED 0x74 bit 7 = LED_ACT, bits 6:0 = (mA - 4) / 2 (bank 1, via CFG0 0xA9 bit 4); ASTATUS 0x94 bit 7 = analog saturation, bits 3:0 = gain code; counts cap at 65535"
 },
